+`context.input_validation` reports measured test accuracy for the exact supplied
+field set. For each target, the server reconstructs the saved held-out split,
+retains those fields, replaces omitted fields with `PatientInput` defaults, and
+evaluates the frozen model at its saved threshold. It returns accuracy, correct
+counts, sample size, 95% Wilson intervals, recall, full-input accuracy and the
+majority-class baseline. These are exploratory cohort results, not confidence
+in an individual prediction. No models are fitted or thresholds selected.
+
+Accuracy is `correct / n_test`; the API returns fractions and the frontend formats
+percentages. Currently each target has 61 held-out rows, stratified by its own
+label, so the selected patients can differ between targets. With Age and Diabetes
+supplied, the check retains those two columns from the cohort and defaults the
+other 52. Patient values are not copied onto the cohort: changing values without
+changing the supplied field set preserves the same test scores.
+
+Validation needs `dataset/dataset.csv` and the saved split metadata. If either is
+unavailable or fails the label/split-size checks, `input_validation.status` is
+`unavailable` and inference still succeeds. Results are cached by field mask, defaults, model
+version/threshold/split and dataset file revision. Restart the backend after
+updating serving artifacts, as for prediction itself.
+
+The dataset must retain the training cohort's rows and ordering to reconstruct
+the held-out split. The current checks do not establish dataset identity with a
+saved content fingerprint. `ARTIFACTS_DIR` changes the model directory, while
+the validation service still reads the repository's `dataset/dataset.csv`.
+The [API contract](../docs/api.md#accuracy-with-available-inputs) documents both
+response states; [Evaluation](../docs/evaluation.md#accuracy-with-available-inputs)
+explains the calculation and limitations.
+
